{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Abraham gave gifts.</b> Not in the language of inheritance at all, so that his instructions would be legally binding." "<b>While he was still alive.</b> And he did not wish to rely on a deathbed directive and the like instruments."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "Reading קַיָּמִים as 'legally binding/valid' — Abraham phrased these as gifts, not inheritance, to ensure they could not be challenged after his death.", 1 "דְּיָיתִיקִי is a loanword (Old French/Old Provençal *ditik/testament*); מִינֵי הַצַּוָּאוֹת = 'kinds of commands/mandates.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:31:38.009486661Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}